  "task.514D125B809C8ABC.title": "Obtain 1 × Rotary Condensentrator",
  "task.514D124EF2AC0D44.title": "Obtain 1 × Electrolytic Separator",
  "task.514D12FFF07FFC19.title": "Obtain 1 × Hohlraum",
  "quest.514D114E75256187.title": "Two fusion fuel streams",
  "quest.514D114E75256187.quest_desc": [
    "Produce deuterium from heavy water and tritium from the lithium line through a Solar Neutron Activator. Prepare the Hohlraum and the required D-T Fuel form for ignition. Separate the streams and verify continuous supply to the reactor."
  ],
  "task.514D12400E1E7B56.title": "1 × Fusion Reactor Controller — not consumed",
  "task.514D1287B291997E.title": "36 × Fusion Reactor Frame — not consumed",
  "task.514D12BAD610257C.title": "3 × Fusion Reactor Port — not consumed",
  "task.514D126FF91F6686.title": "1 × Laser Focus Matrix — not consumed",
  "task.515012E77D162D6C.title": "25 × Reactor Glass — not consumed",
  "task.514D122185675E38.title": "Automatic: Controlled Fusion",
  "quest.514D113E1E8CF8B1.title": "Fusion: fuel, laser, operating cycle",
  "quest.514D113E1E8CF8B1.quest_desc": [
    "The fusion reactor has a fixed rounded 5×5×5 layout: 36 Frames, a Controller, a Laser Focus Matrix, three Ports and 25 Reactor Glass. Follow Mekanism’s diamond-shaped faces rather than filling the corners of a normal cube.",
    "Place the Controller in the centre of the top face. Two ports accept deuterium and tritium separately; the third exports FE. Aim the ignition laser through the Laser Focus Matrix.",
    "The tasks check each material and quantity without consuming it. Hold the kit before placing it, then complete the separate formation or operation check where this quest has one.",
    "Assemble the Fusion Reactor and connect the prepared fuel and laser ignition system to its Laser Focus Matrix. To start the automatic observation, right-click the Fusion Reactor Controller on the formed reactor with your main hand without holding Shift.",
    "Remain in the same dimension within 16 blocks of the controller you clicked. Maintain at least 10 seconds of operation (200 server ticks): the fueled reaction continues and current energy generation is positive. Energy may be sent directly to consumers.",
    "The quest completes while the reactor is running after the full observation interval. Moving beyond 16 blocks, changing dimension, leaving the world or dismantling the reactor interrupts observation; after returning, right-click the controller again. The component kit is checked by the separate item objectives."
  ],
  "task.514D126EA5AE4763.title": "60 × SPS Casing — not consumed",
  "task.514D123CCCB66CA5.title": "3 × SPS Port — not consumed",
  "task.514D120AC974EEB7.title": "1 × Supercharged Coil — not consumed",
  "task.515012190B2C873C.title": "123 × Structural Glass — not consumed",
  "quest.514D114878C1E1BB.title": "SPS: Complete Construction Kit",
  "quest.514D114878C1E1BB.quest_desc": [
    "The SPS uses a fixed rounded 7×7×7 layout: 60 placed SPS Casings, 123 Structural Glass, three SPS Ports and one Supercharged Coil. These are finished construction blocks; casings consumed while crafting the ports are not counted again.",
    "The ports serve polonium input, antimatter output and power. Place the Coil inside, directly behind the power port, and leave the rest of the interior empty.",
    "Inventory tasks verify the kit. Once formed, supply polonium and sufficient FE; the following Antimatter Pellet quest checks the resulting product.",
    "The tasks check each material and quantity without consuming it. Hold the kit before placing it, then complete the separate formation or operation check where this quest has one."
  ],
  "task.513012FCE57931D2.title": "Obtain 1 × Induction Casing",
  "quest.5130116A61A85895.title": "Induction Matrix: the buffer casing",
  "quest.5130116A61A85895.quest_desc": [
    "Build the Induction Matrix shell, add ports and install Cells and Providers inside. Cells determine energy capacity, while Providers determine transfer capability; the two upgrade branches serve different purposes."
  ],
  "task.51301216D0651BC2.title": "Obtain 1 × Induction Port",
  "quest.513011AE27F5BA38.title": "Input and output ports",
  "quest.513011AE27F5BA38.quest_desc": [
    "Induction Ports connect the Matrix to generators and consumers. Configure each port's mode and verify charging and discharging with a small load before connecting the full workshop."
  ],
  "task.513012DCD1614BAD.title": "Obtain 1 × Basic Induction Cell",
  "quest.513011E2552BA5EA.title": "Cell: stored energy",
  "quest.513011E2552BA5EA.quest_desc": [
    "A Basic Induction Cell adds capacity to the Induction Matrix. More capacity bridges peaks or interruptions, but transfer capability still depends on the Providers."
  ],
  "task.5130123BD9C1906D.title": "1 × Basic Induction Provider — not consumed",
  "task.5150128F80EB342D.title": "1 × Basic Induction Cell — not consumed",
  "task.515012DA4B8FFAA2.title": "24 × Induction Casing — not consumed",
  "task.5150121F1B3CD8C2.title": "2 × Induction Port — not consumed",
  "task.51501252B4E2770B.title": "8 × Structural Glass — not consumed",
  "quest.513011ED63C6B222.title": "Induction Matrix: Assemble the Buffer",
  "quest.513011ED63C6B222.quest_desc": [
    "The smallest useful Induction Matrix is 3×4×3: it needs both a Cell and a Provider, so a 1×1×1 interior is insufficient. Use 24 Induction Casings for the frame, eight Structural Glass and two Ports for the remaining faces.",
    "Place one Basic Induction Cell and one Basic Induction Provider inside. Set one port to input and the other to output. The Cell determines capacity; the Provider determines throughput.",
    "The quest verifies the kit. Test operation by connecting a source and consumer, then checking the stored energy in its interface.",
    "The tasks check each material and quantity without consuming it. Hold the kit before placing it, then complete the separate formation or operation check where this quest has one."
  ],
